reOS image and I didn't have time to check if this is true of the latest releases. However, I believe it does work, as @dghubble's examples in coreos-baremetal set up etcd using the domain name as peer URLs, which he says has been working.\n\nMy etcd2.service is located in the gist along with logs. As you can see, I'm getting no validation errors, and etcd proudly proclaims it's listening on a domain name + port. \n\nhttps://gist.github.com/chancez/2b97ae9d2b0c225e98ac964e740f27bd\n","closed_by":{"login":"heyitsanthony","id":16294350,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2Mjk0MzUw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16294350?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/heyitsanthony","html_url":"https://github.com/heyitsanthony","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heyitsanthony/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heyitsanthony/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heyitsanthony/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heyitsanthony/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heyitsanthony/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heyitsanthony/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heyitsanthony/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heyitsanthony/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/heyitsanthony/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/etcd-io/etcd/issues/6336/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/etcd-io/etcd/issues/6336/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}